WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:04.290
- The Surface Duo, a dual screen review

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:06.250
by me, Joanna Stern.

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:09.800
Yep, this is the $1,399 Surface Duo.

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:12.720
Clearly, it's not your
average Android tablet.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:16.590
It's got not one, but two 5.6 inch screens

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:19.150
and a single 11 megapixel camera,

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:21.800
which I'm using to record all
these little selfie videos.

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:23.060
So for this review,

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:25.040
I figured the best thing
I could do was take

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:28.110
your video screen and
split it right in half

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:29.933
to show you what the duo does best.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:34.080
Oh, and yeah, you'll see random
bugs just happen on here.

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:35.683
Opening and closing helps.

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:40.010
But before I explain the good
and bad of having two screens,

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:42.130
let's take a look at this crazy thing.

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:45.530
The Duo has four positions
or as Microsoft calls them...

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:48.215
- This is a book,
posture, posture, posture.

00:00:48.215 --> 00:00:49.250
Do you remember this posture?

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:50.130
I do.

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:52.100
- There's book mode, where the two

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:55.360
pop tart size screens give
you a lot of real estate

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:58.130
and how I ended up using
this thing most of the time.

00:00:58.130 --> 00:01:02.000
There's single screen mode
where you flip one screen back.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.700
There's laptop mode,
though typing like this is

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:06.690
just asking for carpal tunnel

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:10.300
and tent mode, which is
great for watching videos.

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:11.830
I really like the hardware.

00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:15.200
It's compact like a paperback
or a moleskin notebook,

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:16.660
although many of us wouldn't really want

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:19.000
to put these in our pockets.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:22.610
I'm calling it, there's
never been a better time

00:01:22.610 --> 00:01:25.120
for a good old fanny pack.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:26.970
Anyway, great hardware.

00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:29.450
And for $1,400, it should be,

00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:32.440
but software, not so much.

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:34.210
Over the past two weeks of testing,

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:37.980
I encountered loads of
performance issues and bugs.

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:40.550
No, not the crickets you
hear outside my garage

00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:42.973
where we've been shooting this,

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:48.163
the ones that shouldn't exist
on a product this expensive.

00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:50.103
A few days ago,

00:01:50.103 --> 00:01:52.740
Microsoft released a software
update that fixed some of the

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:54.750
issues, but certainly not all,

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:57.710
especially around the slow
and laggy performance.

00:01:57.710 --> 00:02:00.720
The company says it will continue
to deliver monthly updates

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.620
to bring further refinements
to the Surface Duo.

00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:05.290
But when the software cooperated,

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:08.120
here's where two screens were very useful.

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:11.680
Scenario one, one app across two screens.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:14.260
On the left screen here is my Gmail inbox,

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:16.980
on the right, whatever
new email I'm composing.

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:19.360
It's been great whenever I
needed to see the original email

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:20.690
I was responding to.

00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:23.160
On the left here is my
list of notes in One Note

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:26.240
and on the right a blank
page for taking notes.

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:29.140
But you need to buy the
surface pen separately.

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:30.480
PowerPoint, Google Calendar

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:33.770
and other apps also have
this great two screen view.

00:02:33.770 --> 00:02:36.750
Many of Microsoft and Google's
own apps have been optimized

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:38.070
though oddly, not Skype,

00:02:38.070 --> 00:02:40.640
which seems like a no brainer for this.

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:43.190
The companies are working with
other app developers as well.

00:02:43.190 --> 00:02:46.450
Scenario two, an app on each screen

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:49.070
Email on the left, web
browser on the right,

00:02:49.070 --> 00:02:51.640
calendar on the left, email on the right,

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:54.590
YouTube on the left,
One Note on the right,

00:02:54.590 --> 00:02:55.670
you get the point.

00:02:55.670 --> 00:02:59.170
It's great to be able to see
two apps at the same time

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:01.990
as if you were working on a
computer with two monitors.

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:04.480
It's very easy to open one
app on one screen and then

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:06.130
another on the other screen.

00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:09.980
Scenario three, reading on both screens.

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:13.190
Yep, this one's pretty
self explanatory and sweet.

00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:15.220
It's like a real book except you know,

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:17.410
it runs out of battery after a day.

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:20.220
So if Microsoft fixed all
the software bugs tomorrow,

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:22.490
this would be a dream device?

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:24.140
Not quite.

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:25.730
There are just as many scenarios,

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:29.150
if not more, where it doesn't
make sense to have two screens

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:31.210
and definitely not two screens that fold

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:32.890
on top of each other.

00:03:32.890 --> 00:03:35.820
Scenario, one, phone calls.

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:38.680
I don't think I really need
to explain this any further.

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:40.240
If you want to test this out for yourself,

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:42.290
try using one of these things as a phone.

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:48.810
Microsoft does sell these
$200 surface earbuds,

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:50.550
which sounds pretty good

00:03:50.550 --> 00:03:53.630
but look like drink coasters in your ears.

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:56.530
Scenario two, one handed stuff.

00:03:56.530 --> 00:03:57.760
This is awkward.

00:03:57.760 --> 00:03:59.280
This is also awkward,

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:00.640
even though you can adjust the keyboard

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:02.290
to be in the bottom corner.

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:04.875
Scenario three, quick access to the phone.

00:04:04.875 --> 00:04:06.980
You know what's not convenient every time

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:08.170
you want to look at your phone?

00:04:08.170 --> 00:04:09.003
This.

00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:12.880
And especially not when you
want to take a quick photo.

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:15.800
Sure, you can keep the screens
open like this, but again,

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:17.740
see scenario number two.

00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:20.340
Oh yeah, the camera's
not very good either.

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:22.323
So should you buy the Surface Duo?

00:04:24.140 --> 00:04:25.850
Definitely not.

00:04:25.850 --> 00:04:28.220
But that was not the point of this review.

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:30.590
The point of this review was
to show you how Microsoft

00:04:30.590 --> 00:04:33.120
and Google are thinking
differently about the future

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:36.730
of the phone or tablet or
whatever you call this thing.

00:04:36.730 --> 00:04:39.880
Samsung's new Galaxy Fold 2
hints at a similar type of

00:04:41.153 --> 00:04:42.860
future, where our devices
transform when we need them

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:44.690
to do certain things.

00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:46.770
For a while, I thought this
whole thing was a gimmick

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:49.600
and unnecessary but
Microsoft's first entry

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:51.730
has made me think
differently about it all.

00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:54.410
Next time, just make
sure the software works.

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:55.963
Oh, and include a fanny pack.

